title: Case Manager › Active cases › Updated for a payer change
route: /manager
intro: When Payers updates open drafts after a rule change, the cases it redrafted carry a small tag 'Updated for a payer change' with the date, on their 'Being prepared' row and on their tracker row. The tag shows the latest update for a case. Cases that no update lists carry no tag.
dir: TD
also: A case that was already sent (I-2231) has no 'Being prepared' row, so it is tagged in the tracker only. Reset demo data clears the tags.
---
start s1 "Payers › a change is acknowledged and 'Update drafts' is confirmed"
store st1 "Payers records the update\nWhich change, which payer, the IDs of the drafts and the demo-clock time"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Changes › Update drafts after a change"
start s2 "Open Case Manager (Active cases tab)"
decision d1 "Does an update list this case?\n(match on the case ID or draft ID, any letter case)"
process p1 "The newest update for the case is used"
screen t1 "'Being prepared' row\nGrey tag 'Updated for a payer change · 10/20' beside the request line, for example 'Admission request'"
screen t2 "Tracker row\nGrey tag under 'J.M. · 34' in the Case column"
process n1 "No tag"
end e1 "Rows are tagged"
end e2 "Rows as before"

s1 --> st1 --> g1
st1 --> d1
s2 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p1 --> t1 & t2
t1 --> e1
t2 --> e1
d1 -->|No| n1 --> e2
